<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="Good Shit" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"><trk><name>Boreč–Holý vrch–Košťálov winter loop — Boreč, Holý vrch and Košťálov complete loop [planning only — not navigation-grade]</name><desc>From Režný Újezd, climb Boreč by the eastern nature trail and descend by the western nature trail and green markings to Boreč village. Follow yellow markings to Holý vrch’s eastern crossing, make the unmarked summit out-and-back, then continue through Nad Sutomí to the Košťálov castle-footpath out-and-back. Return by green markings and cycle route 25 around Černý les to Boreč village, then yellow village roads to Režný Újezd. The complete three-hill loop is about 11.1 km; allow extra time for the unmarked spur and conditions. Use existing paths, respect vent railings and avoid fenced holes, unsafe masonry and vegetation damage. Carry a current map: this is not one continuously marked loop. Prefer dry, snow-free daylight and calm weather; winter requires every leg to be safe. Village roads carry traffic and lack confirmed continuous protected pavement; the start is not designated parking. Follow closures, forestry and landowner instructions, and postpone if any required leg is unavailable.

Route geometry: © OpenStreetMap contributors, Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0 — https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright; https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/. Source: https://api.openstreetmap.org/api/0.6/map?bbox=13.965,50.472,14.026,50.53. Changes: ordered original-node slices from complete captured OSM walking ways; only duplicate shared junction nodes removed. Canonical display simplifies existing source vertices. No synthetic connectors, private map/guide coordinates or elevations. Two-dimensional planning geometry; not navigation-grade or legal permission.

